# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{blog.html}, nofooter  
= Li Zeng's Blogs

The blog section organizes structured knowledge at the frontier of what I understand into two kinds:

- *Knowledge I have already mastered.* I write it down to organize and deepen it. Writing sharpens my own grasp, and the finished record shows exactly how far I have gotten. When I bring a question to an AI, it can see the edge of my understanding and answer precisely — never re-explaining what I already know, and never leaping so far beyond my reach that the answer slips into hollow talk. I find this a genuinely solid way to improve oneself in the age of AI.
- *Knowledge I have not yet fully absorbed.* I turn it into focused, self-contained tutorials that let me learn efficiently, one step at a time. Where the Study page builds the complete towers of a discipline, these notes are the smaller scaffolds I raise near where I actually stand.

Together, the two kinds make the Blog both a precise record of what I understand and a practical structure for extending that understanding: one consolidates what I know, and the other helps me move beyond it.

